messages.content:
Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: pngrutil.c
Line: 4949
Function: png_progressive_read_reset
Bug type: heap-buffer-overflow
CWE: CWE-122
Explanation: For APNG progressive reading, zlib is configured to write up to PNG_ROWBYTES(png_ptr->pixel_depth, png_ptr->iwidth) + 1 bytes to png_ptr->row_buf, but this function does not ensure that row_buf has been (re)allocated to accommodate a larger next frame. If the new frame is wider than the buffer allocated for the previous frame, a subsequent inflate can write beyond the end of row_buf.

Source context:
```c
     4909:          PNG_ROWBYTES(info_ptr->pixel_depth, png_ptr->width);
     4910:    if (png_ptr->prev_row)
     4911:       memset(png_ptr->prev_row, 0, png_ptr->rowbytes + 1);
     4912: }
     4913: 
     4914: #ifdef PNG_PROGRESSIVE_READ_SUPPORTED
     4915: /* Same as png_read_reset(), but for the progressive reader. */
     4916: void /* PRIVATE */
     4917: png_progressive_read_reset(png_struct *png_ptr)
     4918: {
     4919: #ifdef PNG_READ_INTERLACING_SUPPORTED
     4920:    /* Arrays to facilitate easy interlacing - use pass (0 - 6) as index */
     4921: 
     4922:    if (png_ptr->interlaced)
     4923:    {
     4924:       if (!(png_ptr->transformations & PNG_INTERLACE))
     4925:          png_ptr->num_rows = (png_ptr->height + png_pass_yinc[0] - 1 -
     4926:                               png_pass_ystart[0]) /
     4927:                              png_pass_yinc[0];
     4928:       else
     4929:          png_ptr->num_rows = png_ptr->height;
     4930: 
     4931:       png_ptr->iwidth = (png_ptr->width +
     4932:                          png_pass_inc[png_ptr->pass] - 1 -
     4933:                          png_pass_start[png_ptr->pass]) /
     4934:                         png_pass_inc[png_ptr->pass];
     4935:    }
     4936:    else
     4937: #endif /* PNG_READ_INTERLACING_SUPPORTED */
     4938:    {
